.teach/
.proto/

# The browser MCP server's own output directory, which it creates in
# whatever directory it is run from. It is the same kind of thing as the
# console harness's `console/test-results/`, but it belongs to a separate
# tool that never reads `console/playwright.config.ts`: its location is set
# on the server itself (`--output-dir`), in a configuration that lives
# outside this repository. So the entry stays, and captures taken that way
# are already somewhere git ignores.
.playwright-mcp/

# Screenshots written beside the working tree. Two have been committed by
# accident and removed again (e0d7e78 and #94): a capture lands in the
# repository root whenever a tool is pointed at a relative path before its
# output directory exists, and `git add -A` takes it from there. Root level
# only, because docs and the console keep their images in directories of
# their own, and those are still tracked.
#
# The cause is now configured rather than only caught (issue #99):
# `console/playwright.config.ts` sets `outputDir` to `console/test-results/`,
# and `npm run capture` takes a name rather than a path, so nothing writes
# a capture here to begin with. These three lines are the backstop for the
# tool nobody has configured yet.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# The devenv's generated run directory (ADR-0052): composed supervisor
# configs, the live snapshot, and container state. Everything in it is
# rebuilt by `devenv/devenv up`.
devenv/run/

# Python bytecode from the pack generator (docs/branding/pack/tools/).
__pycache__/

# Build output from the repository's own tools. `go build ./tools/docslint`
# drops a `docslint` executable in whatever directory it is run from, which
# for these is the repository root, and one of those (`vendorlint`) was
# committed and lived in the tree for the whole of the build (issue #122).
# The tools are invoked with `go run`, so nothing needs the file. Anything
# these lines miss is caught by `go run ./tools/binlint`, which fails on any
# tracked file that is a compiled executable.
/binlint
/docslint
/fmtlint
/vendorlint
